Cool, sounds good.  I was thinking I might even solicit feedback at an
earlier stage, one in which the ISO codes and the fu'ivla they form are set
up via some sort of rule...  So, for example, if the language ISO code is
CCV and the family code is VCV, then they go into a CCV'VCV fu'ivla, etc.,
for each of the possible combinations.  I'll have to look and see how doabl=
e
that is; there might still need to be some that would get a different form,
if there is only one or two that have, for example CCC and CCC, it might be
better as an exception than as a rule...

But, yes, I'll certainly let you know as I go along.  I have some free time
today, so hope to start looking at it..

Chris

